    [BugFix][MRV2] Keep replay metadata aligned with FULL graph padding (#18750)
    
    ## Motivation
    
    Fix corrupted and repetitive output from DeepSeek V4.1 Flash W8A8 on
    Ascend A3 when using Model Runner V2 with `FULL_DECODE_ONLY` graphs.
    
    The issue is visible only on the MRv2 FULL graph path. MRv1 and MRv2
    eager execution produce correct results.
    
      ## Root cause
    
    FULL graph attention metadata uses `num_reqs_after_padding`, while
    `EngramModelState` previously passed a `replay_start` tensor sized only
    for the actual request count.
    
    This could make padded graph request rows read invalid replay
    boundaries. In addition, `ReplayAttnMetadata` was injected even when no
    request had an active bounded replay.
    
      ## Changes
    
      - Size `replay_start` to the FULL graph padded request count.
      - Clear padded rows before copying the metadata to device.
    - Inject `ReplayAttnMetadata` only when an active replay boundary
    exists.
    - Add a regression test covering an actual batch padded to the FULL
    graph request shape.
    
      No attention kernel changes are required.
    
      ## Validation
    
      Environment:
    
      - Ascend A3, single node
      - DP2 × TP8 with expert parallelism
      - DeepSeek V4.1 Flash W8A8
      - MRv2, dspark, `FULL_DECODE_ONLY`
      - Prefix caching disabled
    
     Unit tests:
    
      tests/ut/worker/v2/test_deepseek_v41_engram_state.py: 6 passed
      tests/ut/models/test_engram_v2_model_state.py: 30 passed
    
      Real-weight validation:
    
      • At temperature=0, fixed-string, math, and color probes pass 8/8.
    • The previous TheThe and malformed repetitive outputs no longer
    reproduce.
    • At temperature=1, chat probes pass 24/24 and all completion samples
    start with Paris..
    
      Closes #18746
    
